<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of the Intercession on the Nerl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1165">1165</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of the Intercession on the Nerl is a white-stone church near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogolyubovo">Bogolyubovo</a>, outside Vladimir in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, built in 1165 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-bogolyubsky">Andrei Bogolyubsky</a>. Standing in a water meadow near where the Nerl joins the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klyazma">Klyazma</a>, it is famed for its slender, harmonious form and carved façades, and is the best-known monument of the Vladimir-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> school and part of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-the-intercession-on-the-nerl.jpg" alt="Church of the Intercession on the Nerl" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: E.3 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A0%D0%B5%D1%87%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%8F_%D1%86%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B2%D1%8C.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
